<div class="section" aria-labelledby="core-h">

Core finding

<div class="finding-hero">

<span class="interpretation-tag">Interpretation — labeled as such</span>

Pierce County’s major economic institutions derive substantial power
from **government-granted privileges** — federal appropriations, tax
exemption, tribal sovereignty, land grants, and public levies — and
these institutions in turn influence the government that grants those
privileges. This creates a structural interdependence that warrants
scrutiny.

That sentence is the thesis in the only form it survived hostile review.
The sharper versions considered earlier — that the county’s private
sector is “a government-created rentier class,” or that a “growth
machine” is a coordinated operation — were **rejected** in red-team
review as editorializing beyond the evidence. What the records do show
is the direction of the flows below, entity by entity, with sources.

